# mkdir — real-world examples

## Create a directory and all its parents

```sh
mkdir -p foo/bar/baz
```

## Create several directories with brace expansion

```sh
# Create foo/bar and foo/baz
mkdir -p foo/{bar,baz}

# Create foo/bar, foo/baz, foo/baz/zip and foo/baz/zap
mkdir -p foo/{bar,baz/{zip,zap}}
```

## Homelab: media library skeleton on mediaserver

```sh
mkdir -p /srv/plex/{movies,tv,music,photos}
```

## Homelab: dated backup tree, verbose

```sh
mkdir -pv /srv/backups/{daily,weekly,monthly}
mkdir -p "/srv/backups/daily/$(date +%F)"
```

## Create with permissions in one step

```sh
# Private directory (mode applies to the final component)
mkdir -m 700 ~/secrets
```

| Flag | Meaning                                    |
| ---- | ------------------------------------------ |
| -p   | make parents as needed; no error if exists |
| -m   | set permission mode (like chmod)           |
| -v   | print a message for each created directory |
